mment-1556201799","id":1556201799,"issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jax-ml/jax/issues/16080","minimized":null,"node_id":"IC_kwDOCTkjjc5cwcFH","performed_via_github_app":null,"pin":null,"reactions":{"+1":0,"-1":0,"confused":0,"eyes":0,"heart":0,"hooray":0,"laugh":0,"rocket":0,"total_count":0,"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jax-ml/jax/issues/comments/1556201799/reactions"},"updated_at":"2023-05-21T15:03:31Z","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jax-ml/jax/issues/comments/1556201799","user":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/9633?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dlwh/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dlwh/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dlwh/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dlwh/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/dlwh","id":9633,"login":"dlwh","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjk2MzM=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dlwh/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dlwh/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dlwh/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dlwh/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dlwh/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dlwh","user_view_type":"public"}}],"issue":{"active_lock_reason":null,"assignee":null,"assignees":[],"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","body":"### Description\n\nIt looks like zeros_like doesn't preserve sharding information (@sholtodouglas found something different a while back here: https://github.com/google/jax/discussions/12799#discussioncomment-3887579). I feel like it probably should, as Sholto indicated in his post as well.\r\n\r\n```python\r\nimport jax\r\nimport jax.numpy as jnp\r\nfrom jax.experimental.pjit import pjit\r\nfrom jax.sharding import PositionalSharding\r\n\r\n\r\n@pjit\r\ndef init_zeros_like(arr):\r\n    zz = jnp.zeros_like(arr)\r\n    return zz\r\n\r\npos_sharding = PositionalSharding(jax.devices()).reshape((-1, 1))\r\n\r\narr0 = jnp.ones((16, 2))\r\narr0 = jax.device_put(arr0, pos_sharding)\r\n\r\nprint(\"initial array, sharded\")\r\njax.debug.visualize_array_sharding(arr0)\r\n\r\narr1 = init_zeros_like(arr0)\r\n\r\nprint(\"result array, should be sharded but isn't\")\r\njax.debug.visualize_array_sharding(arr1)\r\nassert arr0.sharding.is_equivalent_to(arr1.sharding, 2), (arr0.sharding, arr1.sharding)  # fails\r\n```\r\n\r\n<details><summary>Output showing failure</summary>\r\n<pre>\r\n/opt/homebrew/Caskroom/miniforge/base/envs/levanter/bin/python /Users/dlwh/src/levanter/zeros_like_issue.py \r\ninitial array, sharded\r\n┌───────┐\r\n│ CPU 0 │\r\n├───────┤\r\n│ CPU 1 │\r\n├───────┤\r\n│ CPU 2 │\r\n├───────┤\r\n│ CPU 3 │\r\n├───────┤\r\n│ CPU 4 │\r\n├───────┤\r\n│ CPU 5 │\r\n├───────┤\r\n│ CPU 6 │\r\n├───────┤\r\n│ CPU 7 │\r\n└───────┘\r\nresult array, should be sharded but isn't\r\n┌───────┐\r\n│       │\r\n│       │\r\n│       │\r\n│       │\r\n│ CPU 0 │\r\n│       │\r\n│       │\r\n│       │\r\n│       │\r\n└───────┘\r\nTraceback (most recent call last):\r\n  File \"/Users/dlwh/src/levanter/zeros_like_issue.py\", line 24, in <module>\r\n    assert arr0.sharding.is_equivalent_to(arr1.sharding, 2), (arr0.sharding, arr1.sharding)\r\nAssertionError: (PositionalSharding([[{CPU 0}]\r\n                    [{CPU 1}]\r\n                    [{CPU 2}]\r\n                    [{CPU 3}]\r\n                    [{CPU 4}]\r\n                    [{CPU 5}]\r\n                    [{CPU 6}]\r\n                    [{CPU 7}]]), SingleDeviceSharding(device=CpuDevice(id=0)))\r\n\r\nProcess finished with exit code 1\r\n</pre>\r\n</details>\r\n\n\n### What jax/jaxlib version are you using?\n\njax 0.4.10 jaxlib 0.4.10\n\n### Which accelerator(s) are you using?\n\nCPU (haven't checked TPU/GPU yet)\n\n### Additional system info\n\nPython 3.10.8, MacOS\n\n### NVIDIA GPU info\n\n_No response_","closed_at":"2023-0